     "text": "{\"count\": 2, \"rationale\": \"Blocking h1_1:pivot and h2_1:pivot makes the target unreachable. Blocking h1_1:pivot cuts off h3_1:escalate. It also cuts off h3_0:escalate, an AND step that needs h1_1. Losing h3_0 removes h5_1:access and h4_0:access. Blocking h2_1:pivot cuts off h4_2:access and h3_2:reach, which removes h5_2:pivot. With h4_0, h4_2 and h3_1 all gone, h5_0:reach falls too, so no parent of crown:obtain is reachable. One block cannot be enough. The paths edge0 -> h1_1 -> h3_1 -> h5_0 -> crown and edge0 -> h2_1 -> h3_2 -> h5_2 -> crown share no blockable step, so at least 2 blocks are needed.\"}"
